1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,537
Today is September 21, 2026.

3
00:00:07,537 --> 00:00:13,567
Overnight, the S and P 500 closed higher, with the Nasdaq leading the tech rally.

4
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:16,422
The Dow followed with modest upside.

5
00:00:16,422 --> 00:00:22,280
Ten-year Treasury yields remain the single biggest macro constraint on equity valuations.

6
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:26,741
The September dot plot still signals one more rate hike this year.

7
00:00:26,741 --> 00:00:31,888
Yet the market is pricing only a forty percent probability of an October move.

8
00:00:31,888 --> 00:00:37,451
That gap between Fed hawkishness and market pricing is where all the volatility lives.

9
00:00:37,451 --> 00:00:41,557
This week, a barrage of Fed officials deliver speeches.

10
00:00:41,557 --> 00:00:45,050
Each one is a data point for that October decision.

11
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:49,829
The Treasury is also auctioning six hundred billion in short-term bills.

12
00:00:49,829 --> 00:00:53,542
Plus four hundred forty billion in longer-dated notes.

13
00:00:53,542 --> 00:00:58,505
Weak demand pushes yields higher and compresses growth stock multiples.

14
00:00:58,505 --> 00:01:02,586
Strong demand does the opposite and lifts risk assets.

15
00:01:02,586 --> 00:01:06,361
The Bank of Japan enters a three-day holiday stretch.

16
00:01:06,361 --> 00:01:11,606
Liquidity thins out, and any yen volatility risks triggering intervention.

17
00:01:11,606 --> 00:01:15,356
The dollar-yen pair is flirting with the one-sixty level.

18
00:01:15,356 --> 00:01:21,091
Remember, roughly five trillion dollars in global carry trade flows hinge on that rate.

19
00:01:21,091 --> 00:01:27,402
A sharp yen rally means forced unwinding and amplified volatility across every risk asset.

20
00:01:27,402 --> 00:01:31,655
Now, the China trade talks are the week's biggest catalyst.

21
00:01:31,655 --> 00:01:35,184
He Lifeng leads the delegation through the twenty-third.

22
00:01:35,184 --> 00:01:39,277
The market is pricing a multi-billion dollar tariff reduction.

23
00:01:39,277 --> 00:01:44,559
The optimistic scenario delivers real tariff cuts and eased export controls.

24
00:01:44,559 --> 00:01:50,736
That triggers valuation repair for export-heavy multinationals and lifts risk appetite broadly.

25
00:01:50,736 --> 00:01:55,883
The pessimistic scenario is verbal softening only, no structural change.

26
00:01:55,883 --> 00:02:00,123
In that case, the pre-announcement rally unwinds fast.

27
00:02:00,123 --> 00:02:03,518
Funds take profits and prices retrace.

28
00:02:03,518 --> 00:02:09,094
The key nuance is marginal easing, not a full lifting of semiconductor restrictions.

29
00:02:09,094 --> 00:02:15,246
Any positive signal flows through to AI, pharma, new energy, and rare earths.

30
00:02:15,246 --> 00:02:20,246
On the geopolitical front, the Middle East remains the largest wildcard.

31
00:02:20,246 --> 00:02:24,706
Oil price is the transmission mechanism for every asset class.

32
00:02:24,706 --> 00:02:27,243
Goldman's framework is clear.

33
00:02:27,243 --> 00:02:30,491
Falling oil means all assets rally.

34
00:02:30,491 --> 00:02:36,471
Rising oil means inflation sticks, the Fed stays hawkish, and equities get crushed.

35
00:02:36,471 --> 00:02:40,295
Trump has signaled a major decision on Iran is imminent.

36
00:02:40,295 --> 00:02:46,189
Iran's seven-point ceasefire list reads like a negotiating posture, not a real plan.

37
00:02:46,189 --> 00:02:50,000
Air raid sirens rang in Riyadh for the first time.

38
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,964
Red Sea shipping and Gulf oil export corridors face elevated risk.

39
00:02:54,964 --> 00:02:59,927
Pakistan and Turkey have both voiced military support for Saudi Arabia.

40
00:02:59,927 --> 00:03:04,780
The Houthi forces disclosed a new low-cost cognitive warfare tactic.

41
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:10,687
Special operators scaled cliffs while AI-synthesized voice commands faked a retreat order.

42
00:03:10,687 --> 00:03:15,491
The U.S. has issued security alerts across multiple Middle East countries.

43
00:03:15,491 --> 00:03:18,775
Treat those alerts as high-signal indicators.

44
00:03:18,775 --> 00:03:24,768
If the situation deteriorates, oil spikes fast and the entire rate path reprices.

45
00:03:24,768 --> 00:03:29,057
The Greenland security agreement is a pulse event, not a trend.

46
00:03:29,057 --> 00:03:33,677
The U.S. gained permanent garrison rights and base expansion authority.

47
00:03:33,677 --> 00:03:40,503
Denmark retains sovereignty, but no other nation can build military infrastructure without Washington approval.

48
00:03:40,503 --> 00:03:44,743
Rare earths and Arctic shipping lanes are the strategic prize.

49
00:03:44,743 --> 00:03:47,513
This is election-cycle diplomacy.

50
00:03:47,513 --> 00:03:51,385
It will not move the oil needle or change the equity tape.

51
00:03:51,385 --> 00:03:55,711
Consumer sentiment is at its lowest point since 2025.

52
00:03:55,711 --> 00:04:01,520
Over half of individual investors are bearish, with only twenty-eight point eight percent bullish.

53
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:04,057
Cash positions are elevated.

54
00:04:04,057 --> 00:04:06,716
The Michigan index hit a new low.

55
00:04:06,716 --> 00:04:10,417
Goldman notes the drag is not inflation or income.

56
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:14,621
It is a deeper erosion of public trust and overall well-being.

57
00:04:14,621 --> 00:04:19,045
That is a social-level headwind that no single data print fixes.

58
00:04:19,045 --> 00:04:23,444
Goldman's year-end all-asset rally thesis deserves a close read.

59
00:04:23,444 --> 00:04:28,334
Their core argument is that the bond market has over-priced the hawkish scenario.

60
00:04:28,334 --> 00:04:31,422
The market is pricing four more hikes.

61
00:04:31,422 --> 00:04:33,885
Goldman sees at most two.

62
00:04:33,885 --> 00:04:36,826
The transmission chain is straightforward.

63
00:04:36,826 --> 00:04:42,500
Inflation cools, hike expectations fade, yields drop, bonds rally.

64
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:46,275
Lower rates then lift equities and gold in tandem.

65
00:04:46,275 --> 00:04:48,726
But there is a hard precondition.

66
00:04:48,824 --> 00:04:50,906
Oil must come down.

67
00:04:50,856 --> 00:04:57,755
If oil stays elevated, inflation won't break, the Fed can't stop, and the thesis collapses.

68
00:04:57,755 --> 00:05:03,013
The other risk is an AI capex miss or an unexpected economic downturn.

69
00:05:03,013 --> 00:05:05,697
This is not a one-way bull call.

70
00:05:05,697 --> 00:05:09,275
It is a mean-reversion trade on overdone pessimism.

71
00:05:09,275 --> 00:05:11,714
Turning to the tech complex.

72
00:05:11,714 --> 00:05:14,974
Trump's AI policy is now explicit.

73
00:05:14,974 --> 00:05:17,964
No restrictions on AI development.

74
00:05:17,964 --> 00:05:23,209
He is appointing an AI czar and standing up a dedicated AI task force.

75
00:05:23,209 --> 00:05:26,113
The regulatory posture is permissive.

76
00:05:26,113 --> 00:05:31,150
OpenAI, Google, and Meta are greenlit to keep expanding capex.

77
00:05:31,150 --> 00:05:35,182
AI is being framed as the next industrial revolution.

78
00:05:35,182 --> 00:05:40,427
The stated target is AI contributing twenty-five percent of U.S. GDP.

79
00:05:40,427 --> 00:05:46,652
Musk has publicly argued AI will lift next year's GDP growth from two to four percent.

80
00:05:46,652 --> 00:05:49,226
The policy intent is clear.

81
00:05:49,226 --> 00:05:54,054
Use the AI narrative to anchor the bull market and employment resilience.

82
00:05:54,054 --> 00:05:58,135
The near-term read is positive for the entire AI stack.

83
00:05:58,135 --> 00:06:02,572
Compute, software, and application layers all benefit.

84
00:06:02,572 --> 00:06:05,844
But the medium-term picture is more complex.

85
00:06:05,844 --> 00:06:11,040
AI hardware and semiconductors have already priced in substantial optimism.

86
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,405
Valuations are stretched.

87
00:06:13,405 --> 00:06:16,138
The marginal buyer is getting thinner.

88
00:06:16,138 --> 00:06:20,415
There is a visible rotation underway from hardware into software.

89
00:06:20,415 --> 00:06:26,873
Last week, the S and P software index delivered an average earnings beat of thirteen percent.

90
00:06:26,873 --> 00:06:31,052
Over eighty percent of constituents beat consensus on revenue.

91
00:06:31,052 --> 00:06:35,782
Goldman's cybersecurity basket is up sixty-five percent year to date.

92
00:06:35,782 --> 00:06:38,025
The narrative has shifted.

93
00:06:38,025 --> 00:06:41,383
It is no longer AI destroying software.

94
00:06:41,383 --> 00:06:45,831
It is AI enabling software to unlock new growth vectors.

95
00:06:45,831 --> 00:06:49,275
That is a fundamentally different pricing framework.

96
00:06:49,275 --> 00:06:51,983
But the long-term risk remains.

97
00:06:51,983 --> 00:06:56,420
AI iteration can still disrupt incumbent software models.

98
00:06:56,420 --> 00:07:01,089
And the single biggest risk to the hardware complex is a capex miss.

99
00:07:01,089 --> 00:07:06,040
If hyperscaler spending decelerates, the correction in semis is severe.

100
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:09,447
Now, the three names that matter most today.

101
00:07:09,447 --> 00:07:11,052
Nvidia.

102
00:07:11,052 --> 00:07:13,871
The story is capex dependency.

103
00:07:13,871 --> 00:07:18,822
Every major hyperscaler's spending plan is Nvidia's revenue forecast.

104
00:07:18,822 --> 00:07:21,420
The policy tailwind is real.

105
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:26,591
Washington is explicitly encouraging continued AI infrastructure buildout.

106
00:07:26,591 --> 00:07:30,635
But the valuation has already absorbed a lot of that optimism.

107
00:07:30,635 --> 00:07:35,868
Watch the next earnings cycle for any softness in data center revenue guidance.

108
00:07:35,868 --> 00:07:38,809
Institutional positioning is crowded.

109
00:07:38,809 --> 00:07:43,871
A single negative capex signal from one hyperscaler can trigger a cascade.

110
00:07:43,871 --> 00:07:48,638
On the technical side, the fifty-day moving average is the key support.

111
00:07:48,638 --> 00:07:53,135
A close below that level opens the door to a ten percent drawdown.

112
00:07:53,135 --> 00:07:56,444
Resistance sits at the all-time high cluster.

113
00:07:56,444 --> 00:07:58,662
Here is the risk boundary.

114
00:07:58,662 --> 00:08:03,956
If a Fed speaker hawks the path and oil spikes, de-risk Nvidia first.

115
00:08:03,956 --> 00:08:05,390
Tesla.

116
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:11,824
Musk's public comment that AI lifts GDP growth to four percent is a direct narrative tailwind.

117
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:17,412
The market is trying to reprice Tesla as an AI company, not just an auto company.

118
00:08:17,412 --> 00:08:20,121
That re-rating is the bull case.

119
00:08:20,121 --> 00:08:22,682
The bear case is execution.

120
00:08:22,682 --> 00:08:29,643
Delivery numbers, margin pressure, and the competitive squeeze from Chinese EV makers remain unresolved.

121
00:08:29,643 --> 00:08:32,547
Institutional flows have been choppy.

122
00:08:32,547 --> 00:08:37,400
Hedge fund positioning is split between momentum longs and value shorts.

123
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:41,076
The key technical level is the round-number support zone.

124
00:08:41,076 --> 00:08:45,599
A break below triggers algorithmic selling and accelerates the move.

125
00:08:45,599 --> 00:08:49,263
Above, the prior high is the resistance ceiling.

126
00:08:49,263 --> 00:08:51,738
The risk boundary is clear.

127
00:08:51,738 --> 00:08:57,326
If China talks fail and tariffs tighten, Tesla's China revenue becomes a headwind.

128
00:08:57,326 --> 00:08:58,724
Apple.

129
00:08:58,724 --> 00:09:02,866
Apple is the quiet beneficiary of the software rotation.

130
00:09:02,866 --> 00:09:08,711
Services revenue is growing, and the AI integration roadmap is the next catalyst.

131
00:09:08,711 --> 00:09:13,258
The market has been underweight Apple relative to the broader tech complex.

132
00:09:13,258 --> 00:09:16,677
That underweight is a setup for catch-up flows.

133
00:09:16,677 --> 00:09:20,905
The key driver to watch is the AI feature rollout timeline.

134
00:09:20,905 --> 00:09:27,020
Any confirmation of a meaningful on-device AI capability upgrade re-rates the hardware cycle.

135
00:09:27,020 --> 00:09:31,787
Technically, the two-hundred-day moving average is the institutional floor.

136
00:09:31,787 --> 00:09:34,152
Support is well-defined.

137
00:09:34,152 --> 00:09:37,388
Resistance is the prior earnings-driven high.

138
00:09:37,388 --> 00:09:39,728
The risk is regulatory.

139
00:09:39,728 --> 00:09:44,091
Antitrust exposure in Europe and the U.S. remains an overhang.

140
00:09:44,091 --> 00:09:47,302
If the China talks produce tariff relief,

141
00:09:47,384 --> 00:09:51,316
Apple's supply chain cost structure improves marginally.

142
00:09:51,266 --> 00:09:55,225
That is a secondary benefit, not the primary driver.

143
00:09:55,225 --> 00:09:59,036
The primary driver is AI monetization and
